# .gitattributes — aggressive LF normalization template
#
# Goal: ALL tracked text in the repo is LF. CRLF happens only on
# Windows during checkout (driven by the IDE's .editorconfig), but
# never enters the index. This file is meant to be dropped verbatim
# at the root of each repo (meta, plus the Skymly/* product repos).
#
# Pair this with `core.autocrlf=false`. Every pattern below pins `eol`
# explicitly, so Git must not also guess: with autocrlf=true, any file
# this list does not name gets CRLF on checkout.
#
# Exceptions:
#   - .sln / .slnx: Visual Studio historically emits CRLF. We force LF
#     here, and .editorconfig inherits LF from [*], so editor and index
#     agree. Overriding .sln back to CRLF in .editorconfig turns every
#     save into a whole-file diff.
#   - .cmd / .bat: Windows batch scripts run better with CRLF when
#     invoked from cmd.exe. Keep CRLF (.editorconfig matches).
#   - Anything we know to be binary: marked explicitly. `eol=lf` implies
#     `text`, so the default rule below opts every unnamed file into
#     normalization. Git's NUL-byte sniffing rejects most binaries, but
#     add new binary formats to the list rather than relying on it.
#
# Caveat: a file containing a lone CR (not CRLF) is detected as -text
# and silently skips normalization, which makes it immune to `eol=lf`.
# `git ls-files --eol` reporting `i/-text` on a source file means that,
# not a real binary.
#
# If you find a pattern that needs to be different per repo, drop
# that repo's override into a project-root .gitattributes (this
# file's patterns) and adjust the local normalize script.

# --- Default: treat as text, normalize to LF in the index --------
*               text=auto eol=lf

# --- Documentation / data files ---------------------------------
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.rst           text eol=lf
*.adoc          text eol=lf

# --- Source code ------------------------------------------------
*.cs            text eol=lf
*.csproj        text eol=lf
*.props         text eol=lf
*.targets       text eol=lf
*.xaml          text eol=lf
*.axaml         text eol=lf
*.razor         text eol=lf
*.fs            text eol=lf
*.fsproj        text eol=lf
*.fsx           text eol=lf
*.vb            text eol=lf
*.cpp           text eol=lf
*.h             text eol=lf
*.hpp           text eol=lf
*.c             text eol=lf
*.java          text eol=lf
*.kt            text eol=lf
*.swift         text eol=lf
*.go            text eol=lf
*.rs            text eol=lf

# --- .NET solution files: forced LF -----------------------------
# Visual Studio historically writes these with CRLF. Forcing LF here
# keeps the repo consistent. .editorconfig must not override .sln back
# to CRLF (see header).
*.sln           text eol=lf
*.slnx          text eol=lf
*.slnf          text eol=lf

# Gitignored by the template .gitignore (*.user, *.suo); kept as a
# guard in case one is force-added.
*.csproj.user   text eol=lf
*.suo           binary

# --- Scripting --------------------------------------------------
*.ps1           text eol=lf
*.psm1          text eol=lf
*.psd1          text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.zsh           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.ipynb         text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts: keep CRLF (cmd.exe + classic bat quirks)
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# --- Config / data formats --------------------------------------
*.json          text eol=lf
*.jsonc         text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.config        text eol=lf
*.editorconfig  text eol=lf
*.gitignore     text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# --- Build / lock files ----------------------------------------
# (*.props is declared under "Source code" above.)
package-lock.json text eol=lf
yarn.lock       text eol=lf
pnpm-lock.yaml  text eol=lf

# --- Binary: explicit opt-out -----------------------------------
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.bmp           binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.webp          binary
*.avif          binary
*.psd           binary
*.pdf           binary

# SVG is XML: normalize it so diffs stay readable.
*.svg           text eol=lf

